BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:asian-cultural-council-individual-fellowship-2027@artificialnouveau.git
 hub.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T190955Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261110
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261111
SUMMARY:Deadline: Asian Cultural Council: Individual Fellowship 2027
DESCRIPTION:The Asian Cultural Council's Individual Fellowship funds artist
 s\, scholars and arts professionals from Asia and the U.S. to spend one to
  six months somewhere new or less familiar\, pursuing self-designed resear
 ch and cultural immersion: meeting practitioners\, visiting studios\, muse
 ums\, galleries\, theatres and libraries\, joining workshops and symposia\
 , and doing archival research. ACC is explicit that this is not a producti
 on residency\, not a conference travel grant and not a PR tour. APPLYING J
 OINTLY: two or three people who share research goals can apply together as
  equal partners (one primary applicant\, up to two co-applicants\, no assi
 stant roles)\; the USD 35\,000 cap covers the whole team. Applicants must 
 be citizens or legal permanent residents of an ACC-eligible country\, terr
 itory or region: Afghanistan\, Bangladesh\, Bhutan\, Brunei\, Cambodia\, C
 hina (Mainland)\, East Timor\, Hong Kong SAR\, India\, Indonesia\, Japan\,
  Korea\, Laos\, Macau SAR\, Malaysia\, Mongolia\, Myanmar\, Nepal\, Pakist
 an\, Philippines\, Singapore\, Sri Lanka\, Taiwan\, Thailand\, the U.S. an
 d Vietnam. ELIGIBLE DISCIPLINES (16): architecture (design\, history and t
 heory)\, archaeology\, art history\, arts administration\, arts criticism\
 , conservation\, crafts\, curation\, dance\, ethnomusicology\, film\, lite
 rature\, museum studies\, music\, theater and visual art\; video art and p
 hotography apply under visual art. Additional requirements: at least 21 ye
 ars old by the start\, at least five years of professional experience in a
 n eligible discipline\, no university coursework or teaching during the fe
 llowship\, and confident English if travelling to the U.S. on a J-1 visa. 
 Anyone who has held an ACC grant in the last two calendar years is ineligi
 ble. DESTINATIONS: any eligible country except the one you currently live 
 in\; a place you have lived in for over a year or hold citizenship in need
 s a strong rationale. U.S. fellowships need at least 30 consecutive days a
 nd cannot start before 1 October 2027 because of J-1 processing\; fellowsh
 ips in Asia need 30 cumulative days\, splittable into trips of at least 14
  consecutive days with no more than 14 days between them. ACC sponsors the
  J-1 for U.S. travel\; for Asia you arrange your own visas\, and the fees 
 can go in the budget. WHAT ACC WILL NOT FUND: this is strictly cultural-ex
 change and immersion funding\, not production money. Filming a documentary
 \, researching a planned book or film\, mounting an exhibition\, running a
  concert series\, promotional or PR travel\, equipment purchases and full-
 time residency programmes are all ineligible\, as is funding used only to 
 travel to a single event. TIMELINE: the portal opens 1 October 2026 at 9:5
 9am ET\, applications close 10 November 2026 at 9:59am ET\, and letters of
  recommendation are due 16 November 2026 at 9:59am ET. Review runs Novembe
 r 2026 to April 2027\, notifications go out mid-May 2027\, and all funded 
 activity must take place between 1 August 2027 and 31 December 2028. Apply
  through the GoApply portal\; ACC does not accept email applications. Appl
 icants may apply to only one ACC programme per cycle. No application fee.\
 n\nOrganisation: Asian Cultural Council (ACC)\nLocation: Travel between an
 d within Asia and the United States. Open to citizens and legal permanent 
 residents of ACC-eligible countries\, territories and regions\, including 
 the U.S. You cannot propose travel to the place where you currently live.\
 nAward: Up to USD 35\,000\, the same cap whether you apply alone or jointl
 y with up to two co-applicants. Covers economy airfare\, ground transport\
 , accommodation\, food and daily living costs\, visa fees\, mandatory trav
 el health insurance\, interpretation and costs tied to the exchange activi
 ties. Also included: ACC logistical and research guidance\, introductions 
 to alumni and professionals\, and visa assistance for U.S. travel. No appl
 ication fee.\nDuration: One to six months\, at least 30 days in the destin
 ation\; ACC prefers two months or more in a single place.\n\nMore: https:/
 /www.asianculturalcouncil.org/grant-opportunities?utm_source=artificialnou
 veaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.asianculturalcouncil.org/grant-opportunities?utm_source=art
 ificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Travel between and within Asia and the United States. Open to citi
 zens and legal permanent residents of ACC-eligible countries\, territories
  and regions\, including the U.S. You cannot propose travel to the place w
 here you currently live.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:asian-cultural-council-organization-grant-2027@artificialnouveau.github
 .io
DTSTAMP:20260901T190955Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261110
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261111
SUMMARY:Deadline: Asian Cultural Council: Organization Grant 2027
DESCRIPTION:ACC's Organization Grant funds arts and culture organisations i
 n Asia and the U.S. to run cultural-exchange activities for their staff\, 
 communities and collaborators: sending an activity lead and participants a
 broad\, hosting incoming participants at home\, or both. Up to USD 50\,000
 \, set by ACC against the proposed budget\, activities\, travel duration a
 nd application quality. ELIGIBILITY: the applicant must be a nonprofit\, a
  government-affiliated or sponsored arts or cultural institution (national
  museums\, performing arts centres and the like)\, or an academic or highe
 r-education institution\; legally registered and based in an ACC-eligible 
 country\, territory or region\; and have at least five years of artistic o
 r cultural programming experience. Each application names a primary contac
 t\, an activity lead who runs the work on the ground (can be the same pers
 on)\, and activity participants who may be staff or external collaborators
 . The lead and all participants must be citizens or legal permanent reside
 nts of an eligible location\, and they do not have to share a nationality 
 with each other or with the organisation. Applicants must be citizens or l
 egal permanent residents of an ACC-eligible country\, territory or region:
  Afghanistan\, Bangladesh\, Bhutan\, Brunei\, Cambodia\, China (Mainland)\
 , East Timor\, Hong Kong SAR\, India\, Indonesia\, Japan\, Korea\, Laos\, 
 Macau SAR\, Malaysia\, Mongolia\, Myanmar\, Nepal\, Pakistan\, Philippines
 \, Singapore\, Sri Lanka\, Taiwan\, Thailand\, the U.S. and Vietnam. ELIGI
 BLE DISCIPLINES (16): architecture (design\, history and theory)\, archaeo
 logy\, art history\, arts administration\, arts criticism\, conservation\,
  crafts\, curation\, dance\, ethnomusicology\, film\, literature\, museum 
 studies\, music\, theater and visual art\; video art and photography apply
  under visual art. TRAVEL: one to six months within the grant period\, at 
 least 30 consecutive days in the U.S. or 30 cumulative days in Asia (split
 table into trips of at least 14 consecutive days\, no more than 14 days ap
 art). Travel to a place the lead or participants have spent over a year in
  needs a strong rationale\, and multi-destination or short itineraries are
  less competitive. ACC does not sponsor visas for this programme\; the org
 anisation secures them. WHAT ACC WILL NOT FUND: this is strictly cultural-
 exchange and immersion funding\, not production money. Filming a documenta
 ry\, researching a planned book or film\, mounting an exhibition\, running
  a concert series\, promotional or PR travel\, equipment purchases and ful
 l-time residency programmes are all ineligible\, as is funding used only t
 o travel to a single event. TIMELINE: the portal opens 1 October 2026 at 9
 :59am ET\, applications close 10 November 2026 at 9:59am ET\, and letters 
 of recommendation are due 16 November 2026 at 9:59am ET. Review runs Novem
 ber 2026 to April 2027\, notifications go out mid-May 2027\, and all funde
 d activity must take place between 1 August 2027 and 31 December 2028. App
 ly through the GoApply portal\; ACC does not accept email applications. Ap
 plicants may apply to only one ACC programme per cycle. No application fee
 .\n\nOrganisation: Asian Cultural Council (ACC)\nLocation: Asia and the Un
 ited States. The applicant organisation must be legally registered and bas
 ed in an ACC-eligible country\, territory or region\; activity leads and p
 articipants must be citizens or permanent residents of an eligible locatio
 n\, not necessarily the same one as the organisation.\nAward: Up to USD 50
 \,000. Covers economy airfare\, ground transport\, accommodation\, food an
 d daily living costs\, visa fees\, mandatory travel health insurance\, int
 erpretation and costs tied to the exchange activities. Also included: ACC 
 logistical and substantive guidance\, introductions to alumni\, arts profe
 ssionals and institutions\, and invitations to local ACC events. No applic
 ation fee.\nDuration: One to six months of travel\; at least 30 consecutiv
 e days for U.S. activity\, or 30 cumulative days in Asia.\n\nMore: https:/
 /www.asianculturalcouncil.org/grant-opportunities?utm_source=artificialnou
 veaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.asianculturalcouncil.org/grant-opportunities?utm_source=art
 ificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Asia and the United States. The applicant organisation must be leg
 ally registered and based in an ACC-eligible country\, territory or region
 \; activity leads and participants must be citizens or permanent residents
  of an eligible location\, not necessarily the same one as the organisatio
 n.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:bica-generator-fund-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T190955Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260930
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261001
SUMMARY:Deadline: BICA: Generator Fund 2026 (Kinetic and Potential Grants)
DESCRIPTION:The Generator Fund is BICA's regranting programme for visual ar
 tists in Buffalo and the surrounding two counties\, supported by the Andy 
 Warhol Foundation's Regional Regranting Program. It makes direct project g
 rants to artists rather than to institutions\, and welcomes professional\,
  emerging and experimental practitioners alike. CHOOSING A TRACK: Kinetic 
 Grants (up to USD 5\,000) suit a project with a clear beginning and end\, 
 built around a specific event\, release or presentation\, usually made alo
 ne or with a small team. Potential Grants (up to USD 10\,000) suit an ongo
 ing space\, system or collaborative structure that involves many people an
 d is meant to evolve over time\; these applications also need a sustainabi
 lity plan. ELIGIBILITY: you must live and work in Erie or Niagara County\,
  New York. You can apply as an individual artist\, an informal group or an
  unincorporated collective. NOT ELIGIBLE: 501(c)(3) organisations\; anyone
  receiving a solo exhibition honorarium from BICA in the same fiscal year\
 ; BICA employees\; and anyone who received a Potential Grant in the previo
 us round (they can still apply for a Kinetic Grant). The fund supports vis
 ual arts based projects\, including painting\, sculpture\, installation\, 
 photography\, social practice\, performance art\, video and zines\; projec
 ts rooted primarily in music\, theatre\, dance or literary arts without a 
 strong visual component are not eligible. APPLICATION runs through Submitt
 able and asks for a project title\, a 150-character tagline\, artistic con
 text (up to 250 words)\, a full project description (up to 500 words\, the
  most heavily weighted part\, expected to cover where the project happens 
 or how the public accesses it\, a timeline with key milestones\, the audie
 nce and how you will reach them\, and the people involved)\, a budget on B
 ICA's project budget sheet covering expenses\, in-kind support and income\
 , work samples (images\, video or PDFs of past work and a sense of what is
  to come) and a CV. SUPPORT before the deadline includes a virtual info se
 ssion on 12 August 2026 at 5:30 pm\, an in-person info session at BICA on 
 5 September 2026 at 3:30 pm (followed by a budget and CV workshop led by N
 ando Alvarez-Perez)\, one-on-one office hours with the Generator Fund coor
 dinator on Thursdays\, Fridays and Saturdays through August and September\
 , and group work sessions at BICA School Lab (30B Essex St) on 19 and 26 S
 eptember 2026\, 12 to 5 pm. Applications submitted a week or more early ma
 y receive feedback and be reopened for edits.\n\nOrganisation: Buffalo Ins
 titute for Contemporary Art (BICA)\nLocation: Applicants must live and wor
 k in Erie or Niagara County\, New York\, USA. BICA is at 30D Essex Street\
 , Buffalo\, NY 14213.\nAward: Two grant types: Kinetic Grants of up to USD
  5\,000 for short-term\, public-facing visual arts projects (exhibitions\,
  performances\, installations\, workshops\, publications)\, and Potential 
 Grants of up to USD 10\,000 for long-term\, collaborative or platform-buil
 ding projects (artist-run spaces\, recurring events\, media platforms and 
 other structures that extend beyond a single outcome). No application fee.
  The fund is part of the Andy Warhol Foundation's Regional Regranting Prog
 ram.\nDuration: Applications open 1 August 2026 and close 30 September 202
 6\; jurors review in October and meet in November\; grantees are notified 
 in December 2026\; cheques are handed over in January 2027 at the Meet the
  Grantees event\; proposed projects are to be completed by 31 December 202
 7.\n\nMore: https://www.generatorfund.org/apply?utm_source=artificialnouve
 augrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.generatorfund.org/apply?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantde
 sk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Applicants must live and work in Erie or Niagara County\, New York
 \, USA. BICA is at 30D Essex Street\, Buffalo\, NY 14213.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:warhol-foundation-exhibition-support-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T190955Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260902
SUMMARY:Deadline: Andy Warhol Foundation: Exhibition Support (Fall 2026 rou
 nd)
DESCRIPTION:Supports solo\, two-person and thematic group exhibitions of co
 ntemporary visual art. The Foundation explicitly prioritises artists whose
  work is under-recognised and whose practices are experimental or hard to 
 categorise\, which makes it a genuine route for media arts\, digital cultu
 re and art-and-science exhibitions rather than a blue-chip-only fund. Gran
 ts of USD 60\,000 to 100\,000 cover direct exhibition costs including arti
 st fees\, new commissions\, catalogue production and artist-designed publi
 c programming\, but not staff salaries. Applicants may request no more tha
 n 25 percent of total direct costs. The proposal is a roughly three-page c
 uratorial letter plus detailed direct-cost budget\, organisational budget 
 and IRS documentation. Deadlines are 1 March and 1 September annually\, wi
 th notifications 1 July and 1 January. IMPORTANT: this is a postmark or em
 ail-timestamp deadline\, not a portal deadline. Fiscal sponsors are explic
 itly not accepted\; the applicant must hold its own IRS ruling letter. The
  six-month-to-two-year timing rule is strict\, so a September 2026 applica
 tion suits exhibitions programmed from mid-2027 onward.\n\nOrganisation: T
 he Andy Warhol Foundation for the Visual Arts\nLocation: Applicant's own v
 enue. US-based 501(c)(3) required\; international organisations must first
  submit a letter of inquiry before any proposal is accepted.\nAward: USD 6
 0\,000 to 100\,000. Direct costs only (artist payments\, catalogue and pub
 lication\, artist-designed public programmes)\; staff salaries excluded. R
 equest must not exceed 25 percent of total direct project costs\, which fu
 nctions as a de facto 75 percent co-financing requirement. No application 
 fee.\nDuration: Exhibition must open between 6 months and 2 years after no
 tification.\n\nMore: https://warholfoundation.org/grants/application-guide
 lines/exhibition-support/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium
 =referral
URL:https://warholfoundation.org/grants/application-guidelines/exhibition-s
 upport/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Applicant's own venue. US-based 501(c)(3) required\; international
  organisations must first submit a letter of inquiry before any proposal i
 s accepted.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:warhol-foundation-multiyear-program-support-2026@artificialnouveau.gith
 ub.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T190955Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260902
SUMMARY:Deadline: Andy Warhol Foundation: Multi-year Program Support (Fall 
 2026 round)
DESCRIPTION:This is the closest thing in US foundation philanthropy to core
  support for an organisation running an ongoing public programme\, as oppo
 sed to a single exhibition. It funds a two-year slate of exhibitions\, res
 idencies\, public art\, screenings\, performances\, lectures and publicati
 ons\, which means a recurring festival or convening series can be underwri
 tten here. Grants are USD 60\,000 to 100\,000 over two years and may not e
 xceed 25 percent of annual operating budget. The Foundation states a prefe
 rence for organisations supporting artists with experimental\, hard-to-cat
 egorise practices\, putting digital culture\, sound art and art-and-scienc
 e programmers squarely in scope. Applications require a forward programme 
 schedule covering at least the twelve months after the award\, a three-pag
 e narrative focused specifically on how artists benefit (the stated centra
 l evaluation criterion)\, a full one-year organisational budget and 501(c)
 (3) documentation. Deadlines are 1 March and 1 September\, notifications 1
  July and 1 January. Fiscal sponsors are not accepted. Organisations that 
 received a Multi-year grant within the past year are ineligible\, and prop
 osals centred on anniversaries\, relocations or major renovations are expl
 icitly discouraged.\n\nOrganisation: The Andy Warhol Foundation for the Vi
 sual Arts\nLocation: Programming delivered by the applicant organisation. 
 US 501(c)(3) required\; international organisations must submit a letter o
 f inquiry first.\nAward: USD 60\,000 to 100\,000 across two years. Request
  must not exceed 25 percent of the organisation's annual operating budget.
  No formal match\, but the 25 percent cap means the balance must come from
  elsewhere. No application fee.\nDuration: Two years of programming\, begi
 nning after the 1 January 2027 notification.\n\nMore: https://warholfounda
 tion.org/grants/application-guidelines/multi-year-program-support/?utm_sou
 rce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://warholfoundation.org/grants/application-guidelines/multi-year-p
 rogram-support/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Programming delivered by the applicant organisation. US 501(c)(3) 
 required\; international organisations must submit a letter of inquiry fir
 st.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:warhol-foundation-small-scale-project-grants-2026@artificialnouveau.git
 hub.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T190955Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260902
SUMMARY:Deadline: Andy Warhol Foundation: Project Grants for Small-Scale Or
 ganizations (Fall 2026 round)
DESCRIPTION:Launched in February 2026 as an expansion of the Foundation's p
 rogramme to reach organisations too small for the Exhibition Support and M
 ulti-year strands\, and it is the single most relevant new US scheme for s
 mall media-arts festivals. It funds visual arts projects with a public com
 ponent\, explicitly naming film festivals\, exhibitions\, installations\, 
 residencies and interdisciplinary collaborations. Grants are USD 20\,000 t
 o 30\,000 toward direct costs. The hard gate is the USD 200\,000 annual op
 erating budget ceiling plus US 501(c)(3) status held directly by the appli
 cant\, not via a fiscal sponsor. The Foundation states it assesses creativ
 e risk-taking and the growth of participating artists rather than communit
 y impact metrics\, which suits experimental sound and digital culture prog
 ramming. Proposals are a maximum of three pages plus a one-year operating 
 budget\, a project budget and IRS documentation. Deadlines are 1 March (pr
 ojects begin 1 July or later) and 1 September (projects begin 1 January or
  later). Youth-focused projects are ineligible. One project per round\, an
 d grantees must wait a year after project completion and final reporting b
 efore reapplying.\n\nOrganisation: The Andy Warhol Foundation for the Visu
 al Arts\nLocation: Applicant's own venue or programme\, with a mandatory p
 ublic component. US-based only.\nAward: USD 20\,000 to 30\,000 toward dire
 ct costs such as artist payments and production. No application fee.\nDura
 tion: Project must complete within one year of notification\; September-ro
 und projects may begin 1 January 2027 or later.\n\nMore: https://warholfou
 ndation.org/grants/application-guidelines/project-grants-for-small-scale-o
 rganizations/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://warholfoundation.org/grants/application-guidelines/project-gran
 ts-for-small-scale-organizations/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&ut
 m_medium=referral
LOCATION:Applicant's own venue or programme\, with a mandatory public compo
 nent. US-based only.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:teiger-foundation-hosting-grant-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T190955Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260909
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260910
SUMMARY:Deadline: Teiger Foundation: Hosting Grant (September 2026 quarterl
 y deadline)
DESCRIPTION:Funds US organisations to present curator-led contemporary visu
 al art exhibitions and projects that originated elsewhere\, on condition t
 he presenting institution meaningfully adapts the project to its own conte
 xt. Teiger's remit covers group exhibitions\, single-artist surveys\, part
 icipatory and community-engaged projects\, digital exhibitions\, and live 
 and virtual performance\, making it one of very few US funders that will d
 irectly finance media-art and performance programming at organisational le
 vel. Requests are fixed at USD 50\,000 or USD 75\,000 with up to 30 percen
 t for indirect costs\, and there is no minimum organisation budget size\, 
 with smaller organisations explicitly favoured for infrastructure support.
  Hosting deadlines are quarterly: 9 September 2026 and 9 December 2026\, b
 oth 17:00 ET\, each mapped to a defined project-opening window roughly a y
 ear out. IMPORTANT: re-presenting a touring project unchanged is explicitl
 y not competitive\; the curatorial adaptation is the substance of the appl
 ication. US 501(c)(3) status is required and the fund is not open to indiv
 iduals or non-US organisations. Teiger's larger biennial Call for Proposal
 s is not running in 2026 and next opens in autumn 2026 with an early-2027 
 deadline.\n\nOrganisation: Teiger Foundation\nLocation: United States. The
  presenting organisation must be US-based\, though the originating project
  may have come from anywhere in the world.\nAward: USD 50\,000 or USD 75\,
 000 (fixed request tiers\, applicant chooses). Up to 30 percent may cover 
 indirect and overhead costs. Organisations with annual budgets under USD 3
 .5 million receive special consideration for infrastructure costs. No matc
 hing requirement. No application fee.\nDuration: Roughly 12 months\; the 9
  September 2026 deadline covers projects opening between 1 April 2027 and 
 31 March 2028.\n\nMore: https://teigerfoundation.org/what-we-fund-how-to-a
 pply/hosting?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://teigerfoundation.org/what-we-fund-how-to-apply/hosting?utm_sour
 ce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:United States. The presenting organisation must be US-based\, thou
 gh the originating project may have come from anywhere in the world.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:alabama-clotilda-memorial-public-art-commission-2026@artificialnouveau.
 github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T190955Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260809
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260810
SUMMARY:Deadline: Alabama Historical Commission: Clotilda Memorial Public A
 rt Commission
DESCRIPTION:The Alabama Historical Commission\, working with public-art con
 sultancy Forecast Public Art\, seeks proposals for a major memorial artwor
 k honoring the survivors of the Clotilda\, the last known ship to illegall
 y traffic enslaved Africans to the United States (1860). The memorial will
  convey the survivors' lives and legacies and be developed through collabo
 rative community engagement with historic Africatown\, the community found
 ed by Clotilda survivors\, and the broader diaspora. ELIGIBILITY: open to 
 artists of all disciplines\, including time-based and media artists\; indi
 viduals and teams\; open internationally. BUDGET: USD 2\,000\,000 total pr
 oject budget. DEADLINE: 9 August 2026\, 11:59pm CST. Applications are hand
 led through the CODAworx RFQ platform\; find the Clotilda Memorial listing
  in the CODAworx opportunities index. Verify the listing details on CODAwo
 rx before applying.\n\nOrganisation: Alabama Historical Commission (with F
 orecast Public Art)\nLocation: Africatown\, Mobile\, Alabama\, USA\; open 
 to artists internationally.\nAward: USD 2\,000\,000 total project budget f
 or a paid public art commission. No application fee.\nDuration: Permanent 
 public art commission\n\nMore: https://www.codaworx.com/rfp/?utm_source=ar
 tificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.codaworx.com/rfp/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm
 _medium=referral
LOCATION:Africatown\, Mobile\, Alabama\, USA\; open to artists internationa
 lly.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:100-voices-of-florida-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T190955Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260920
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260921
SUMMARY:Deadline: 100 Voices of Florida Film Grant
DESCRIPTION:100 Voices of Florida is a grant for filmmakers and screenwrite
 rs that awards up to USD 5\,000 in unrestricted funds\, which winners can 
 use for finishing funds\, festival submission fees\, cast and crew reimbur
 sements\, production\, or anything else. Applicants submit either a short 
 film (under twenty minutes) or a script (twenty pages or less)\; films in 
 other languages must include accurate English subtitles\, and scripts must
  be in English. The grant is open to writers\, directors\, and producers w
 ho are at least 18 years old\, and creative teams may submit\, though only
  one entrant receives the award. A panel of judges with professional filmm
 aking experience evaluates entries\, and the winner also receives a meetin
 g with an industry professional. The deadline for the current cycle is Sep
 tember 20\, 2026.\n\nOrganisation: 100 Voices of Florida\nLocation: Florid
 a\, United States\nAward: Up to USD 5\,000 (unrestricted) USD 25 applicati
 on fee with a Florida connection\, USD 35 without\nDuration: One-time gran
 t\n\nMore: https://www.100vof.com/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&u
 tm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.100vof.com/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_mediu
 m=referral
LOCATION:Florida\, United States
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:rauschenberg-medical-emergency-grants-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T190955Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261117
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261118
SUMMARY:Deadline: Rauschenberg Medical Emergency Grants
DESCRIPTION:The Rauschenberg Medical Emergency Grants\, administered by the
  New York Foundation for the Arts on behalf of the Robert Rauschenberg Fou
 ndation\, provide one-time grants of up to USD 5\,000 to help artists in f
 inancial need cover recent unexpected medical\, dental\, and mental health
  emergencies. The program is open to generative visual and media artists a
 nd choreographers working in visual arts\, film\, video\, electronic and d
 igital arts\, and choreography who live anywhere in the United States\, th
 e District of Columbia\, a Tribal Nation\, or a U.S. Territory. Applicants
  must be artists in financial need\, with adjusted gross income at or belo
 w USD 80\,000 for an individual or USD 160\,000 for joint filers\, and mus
 t not have received a Rauschenberg Medical or Dancer Emergency Grant in th
 e past five years. Eligible expenses include emergency medical bills\, dia
 gnostics\, consultations\, therapy\, prescription medications\, emergency 
 dental care\, and transportation to appointments. The grant does not cover
  lost wages\, general living expenses\, or care for anyone other than the 
 artist. Applications are accepted during defined cycles\, with the current
  cycle running roughly from late October to mid November.\n\nOrganisation:
  New York Foundation for the Arts (NYFA) / Robert Rauschenberg Foundation\
 nLocation: United States (remote application)\nAward: One-time grants up t
