UID:moorhead-call-public-art-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T190955Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260904
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260905
SUMMARY:Deadline: City of Moorhead: 2026 Call for Public Art (Movable Inter
 active Piece)
DESCRIPTION:The City of Moorhead is seeking proposals for an inspirational\
 , movable public artwork to be installed at rotating locations across the 
 city. Interactive elements are explicitly encouraged\, with kinetic sculpt
 ure\, digital installation and tactile elements named as examples. Strong 
 proposals invite public participation\, promote creativity and youth engag
 ement\, are safe for all members of the public\, are durable enough for ye
 ar-round outdoor conditions\, and draw people to gather. Submissions are r
 eviewed and ranked by the Artist Review Team\, whose recommendation passes
  to the Art and Culture Commission and then to City Council for the final 
 decision. Questions go to art@moorheadmn.gov. Proposals are due by 10:00am
  on Friday 4 September 2026.\n\nOrganisation: City of Moorhead\, Minnesota
 \nLocation: Moorhead\, Minnesota\, USA. The piece will be sited at differe
 nt locations throughout the city. No geographic eligibility restriction is
  stated in the call\, so non-US artists appear eligible\, but this is not 
 confirmed in writing.\nAward: Not published. The call announcement states 
 no budget\, commission amount or artist fee\, and the linked Request for A
 rt document could not be retrieved. Confirm the budget with art@moorheadmn
 .gov before investing time in a proposal. No application fee is mentioned.
 \nDuration: Single commission\; timeline not published\n\nMore: https://ww
 w.moorheadmn.gov/news/posts/2026-call-for-public-art/?utm_source=artificia
 lnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.moorheadmn.gov/news/posts/2026-call-for-public-art/?utm_sou
 rce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Moorhead\, Minnesota\, USA. The piece will be sited at different l
 ocations throughout the city. No geographic eligibility restriction is sta
 ted in the call\, so non-US artists appear eligible\, but this is not conf
 irmed in writing.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:legalization-project-immigrant-content-creators-2026@artificialnouveau.
 github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T190955Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260817
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260818
SUMMARY:Deadline: The Legalization Project: Immigrant Content Creators Prog
 ram 2026-27
DESCRIPTION:The Legalization Project is running a nine-month programme for 
 experienced content creators who want to make engaging\, accessible work a
 bout U.S. immigration law\, policy and the issues affecting immigrant comm
 unities. Rather than commissioning one-off pieces\, it pairs a USD 10\,000
  stipend with actual legal grounding: training in U.S. immigration law and
  policy\, ongoing updates from immigration attorneys and advocates\, and c
 ontinuous feedback on the content you make. This suits creators already wo
 rking in video\, social or short-form documentary who want to report accur
 ately on a fast-moving legal area rather than guess at it. ELIGIBILITY: ex
 perienced content creators who are immigrants. The programme is explicitly
  open to immigrants of ALL statuses. APPLICATION: preliminary applications
  are due 17 August 2026\, through the programme page at legalizationprojec
 t.notion.site/icc-program (also circulated as bit.ly/icc-program). Being a
  preliminary application\, expect a second stage after this date.\n\nOrgan
 isation: The Legalization Project\nLocation: United States focus (content 
 covers U.S. immigration law and policy). Programme delivery format not spe
 cified in the call.\nAward: USD 10\,000 stipend\, plus training in U.S. im
 migration law and policy\, regular updates from immigration attorneys and 
 advocates\, and ongoing feedback and support on your content. No applicati
 on fee.\nDuration: Nine months\n\nMore: https://legalizationproject.notion
 .site/icc-program?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referra
 l
URL:https://legalizationproject.notion.site/icc-program?utm_source=artifici
 alnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:United States focus (content covers U.S. immigration law and polic
 y). Programme delivery format not specified in the call.
END:VEVENT
