SUMMARY:Deadline: Emerging Traditional Artists Program 2026
DESCRIPTION:South Arts' Emerging Traditional Artists Program supports folk 
 and traditional artists in the early stages of their careers with USD 5\,0
 00 each\, plus professional development workshops and peer mentorship at n
 o cost. The money is for learning: training\, networking and promotion. Re
 cipients also record an interview about their art practice. ELIGIBILITY: i
 ndividual practitioners early in their careers\, at least 18 by the deadli
 ne\, US citizens or lawfully authorised residents\, who have lived for at 
 least two years in designated Appalachian Regional Commission or Delta Reg
 ional Authority counties within Alabama\, Georgia\, Kentucky\, Louisiana\,
  Mississippi\, North Carolina\, South Carolina or Tennessee\, or who are m
 embers of state or federally recognised Native American tribes. Applicants
  must demonstrate a high level of skill in\, commitment to\, and leadershi
 p in their traditional art form. Deadline 30 September 2026 at 5:00pm ET.\
 n\nOrganisation: South Arts\nLocation: Designated Appalachian Regional Com
 mission and Delta Regional Authority counties in Alabama\, Georgia\, Kentu
 cky\, Louisiana\, Mississippi\, North Carolina\, South Carolina and Tennes
 see\, USA.\nAward: USD 5\,000 per awardee\, paid as a single lump sum at t
 he start of the award period\, to fund learning opportunities including tr
 aining\, networking and promotion. Recipients also take part in virtual wo
 rkshops and peer mentorship at no cost\, and record an interview about the
 ir practice. No application fee.\nDuration: Award period with accompanying
  workshops and peer mentorship\n\nMore: https://www.southarts.org/grants-o
 pportunities/emerging-traditional-artists-program?utm_source=artificialnou
 veaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
